@attribute [Route(GlobalValues.Path_Theming_CSS_Base_Variables)]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Page_Title_Theming_CSS_Base_Variables</PageTitle>

<h1 class="page-heading">@GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Theming_CSS_Base_Variables</h1>

<p>The following css custom properties (variables) are used for all components.</p>
<p>
    A component may define its own variables which can accept the base variable values
    or override them, as and when necessary; this allows you very fine grained control.
</p>
<p>
    Changing one base variable will ripple through the system and change everything, but you can, at various stages override this
    behaviour in order to apply a specific value to a specific component without effecting the others.
</p>
<p>
    <b>Note: </b>More base variables may be added and/or some default values may be changed but only if they are not currently in use by a released component.
</p>
<section class="code-table">

    <h2 id="base-outline-variables" class="code-table__heading">Base outline variables</h2>

    <table aria-labelledby="base-outline-variables" >

        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Variable Name</th>
                <th scope="col">Default Value</th>
                <th scope="col">Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>--br-comp-all-outline-style</td>
                <td>solid</td>
                <td>The style type of the outline.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>--br-comp-all-outline-width</td>
                <td>var(--br-unit-outline-2)</td>
                <td>The width of the outline.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>--br-comp-all-outline-offset</td>
                <td>var(--br-unit-outline-offset-2)</td>
